; stashpark.eval - a level PARKED and then live again IN PLACE keeps no stash of
; itself, and a game begun on ANOTHER level keeps the edit it left behind
; (code-review C298, C308). Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 31, on a scratch
; copy of dungeon-demo; `stashpark` is renamed to this worktree's save.
;
; 1. PARKED, THEN BACK IN PLACE. A save made on crypt1; a wall painted at 9,1,
;    not saved; then `leave` for the world map, which PARKS crypt1 and stashes
;    its map (it differs from its file). Loading the save lands on crypt1
;    itself, in place, so no level load consumes that stash - and it used to
;    stand all the while, under the live level's own stem. The square is put
;    back as filed (its looks erased, floor and ceiling repainted as the file
;    has them), so the level reads clean; a savemap then wrote the stale stash
;    over what it had just written of the live level, the stairs stashed nothing
;    to replace it, and going back brought the wall back. Now the load in place
;    drops it: nothing is stashed after the load, the savemap writes crypt1
;    once, the stairs stash nothing and going back finds the floor.
; 2. A GAME BEGUN ELSEWHERE (C298's second trigger). A wall painted at 10,1 on
;    crypt1, then `newgame`, which begins on eval_arena by the "throwaway
;    baseline" door that used to drop the map with the dynamic state: crypt1's
;    map is stashed on the way out, savemap writes it, going back finds it.
; EditorTest reads crypt1.map: 9,1 a floor again, 10,1 a wall.

logecho on
reset
goto crypt1
save stashpark
echo --- before ---
mapinfo
stashes
editor drag walls wall_marble 9 1
mappage close
echo --- painted ---
mapinfo
stashes
leave
echo --- parked ---
stashes
load stashpark
echo --- loaded ---
stashes
editor erase 9 1
editor drag floors floor_cobble_mossy 9 1
editor drag ceilings ceiling_rock_layered 9 1
mappage close
echo --- put back ---
mapinfo
stashes
savemap
goto crypt2
echo --- left ---
stashes
goto crypt1
echo --- back ---
mapinfo
stashes
editor drag walls wall_marble 10 1
mappage close
echo --- painted again ---
mapinfo
stashes
newgame
echo --- new game ---
stashes
savemap
goto crypt1
echo --- returned ---
mapinfo
stashes
echo --- end ---
